# https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "19/05/21" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HIQA National Standards for the Prevention and Control of Healthcare-Associated Infections 2017" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Micro-organisms that pose a significant risk of transmission to non-infected patients or staff, resulting in colonisation or healthcare-associated infection, or that pose a significant risk of transmission to non-infected people in the wider population or community" .
<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#AlertOrganism> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#> .
