<https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#HomeBasedDialysis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Dialysis that is performed at home including peritoneal dialysis or home haemodialysis. Peritoneal dialysis is a treatment for kidney failure which uses the body’s natural membrane in the abdominal cavity to clean the blood. Home haemodialysis is a treatment in which the blood is cleaned outside the body by a machine that passes blood across a filte" .
